msgid "pio check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:17
msgid "Helper command for :ref:`check`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:19
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:22
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:29
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:31
msgid ""
"Perform static analysis check on PlatformIO based project. By default :ref:"
"`check_tool_cppcheck` analysis tool is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:33
msgid "More details about PlatformIO :ref:`check`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:36
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:43
msgid "Process specified environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:50
msgid ""
"You can specify which source files or folders should be included/excluded "
"from check process. By default only :ref:`projectconf_pio_src_dir` and :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_include_dir` are checked. Multiple ``--src-filters`` "
"options and `GLOB Patterns <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Glob_(programming)>`_ are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:55
msgid ""
"Example: ``pio check --src-filters=\"+<src/app/>\" --src-filters=\"-<src/app/"
"uart/>\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:60
msgid ""
"Specify additional flags that need to be passed to the analysis tool. If "
"multiple tools set in :ref:`projectconf_check_tool` option, the flags are "
"passed to all of them. Individual flags for each tool can be added using a "
"special suffix with the tool name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:67
msgid "Flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:68
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:70
msgid "``--addon=<addon>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:71
msgid "Execute addon. i.e. cert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:73
msgid "``-D<ID>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:74
msgid "Define preprocessor symbol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:76
msgid "Multiple ``--flags`` options are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:78
msgid ""
"Example: ``pio check --flags \"-DDEBUG cppcheck: --std=c++11 --"
"platform=avr8\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:83
msgid ""
"Specify the :ref:`check_severity` types which will be reported by the :ref:"
"`check_tools`. Possible values described in :ref:`check_severity` section. "
"Multiple ``--severity`` options are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:87
msgid "Example: ``pio check --severity=high``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:92
msgid ""
"Specify the path to project directory. By default, ``--project-dir`` is "
"equal to the current working directory (``CWD``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:98
msgid "Process project with a custom :ref:`projectconf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:103
msgid ""
"Return the output in `JSON <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON>`_ format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:108
msgid ""
"Fail (exit with non-zero code) if there is a defect found with specified "
"severity. By default exit code is the same as the exit code returned by a "
"tool selected for performing check. Possible values described in :ref:"
"`check_severity` section. Multiple ``--fail-on-defect`` options are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:113
msgid "Example: ``pio check --fail-on-defect=low --fail-on-defect=medium``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:118
msgid ""
"Exclude underlying third-party packages from the checking process. By "
"default, PlatformIO passes frameworks and toolchains include paths required "
"by internal analysis tools to properly analyze project sources. Some of the "
"supported analysis tools use their own preprocessor which may fail to parse "
"perfectly valid code and thus provide empty or partial check reports. This "
"option is useful when developers have no control over this third-party code "
"and want to perform analysis at least on project sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:125
msgid "Example: ``pio check --skip-packages``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:130
msgid ""
"Suppress progress reporting and show only defects with ``high`` severity. "
"See :ref:`check_severity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:136
msgid "Show detailed information when processing environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_check.rst:138
msgid ""
"This option can also be set globally using :ref:`setting_force_verbose` "
"setting or by environment variable :envvar:"
"`PLATFORMIO_SETTING_FORCE_VERBOSE`."
msgstr ""

